The Castle was, hmm.., no real danger but a pain. Cowardly genocided
all the liches before the first contact, but a titan took over their
job. He unblessed my bag of holding, cursed many pieces of my armor,
and worst, also my two-handed Cleaver, summoned E-resistant minotaur
and other creatures. The forecasts suggested that I won't survive
three turns in this hostile environment and to use the two charges of
the wand of teleportation on the titan and the minotaur.

So far so good, the situation is under control again. But it was
astonishing how specifically the titan cursed my sensible equipment.

Something that surprised me a bit; a prayer (while weak from hunger)
just removed the curse from my weapon, but not from my armor; somehow
I thought it would fix all the curses on worn items. (I rarely used to
ask my god for help, but in this case, both hands weld to Cleaver...)

My plan was to use a rubber chicken to dispose the titan (so that I am
not bothered by him any more when I have to pass this place again).
But he stood on a moat square in the lower right corner of the castle
and did not come close, but departed further. (Was he so scared by the
teleportation? ;-)

